// FILE: versioning_law_v1.law
/*******************************************************************************
 *                           AVIS.ARTIFACT HEADER
 * TYPE: LAW
 * CLASS: VERSIONING-LAW
 * NAME: VERSIONING-LAW-V1
 * VERSION: 1.00
 * ROLE: Rules for Governance Artifact Evolution
 * ENGINE: AVIS-2026 / AIFVS-MODE
 * ORIGIN: /mercwar01/law/versioning_law_v1.law
 *******************************************************************************
 * [PURPOSE]
 * Define how governance artifacts evolve, update, and maintain continuity
 * within the AVIS ecosystem.
 *
 * [VERSIONING PRINCIPLES]
 * 1. Semantic Structure:
 *    Use MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH format.
 *
 * 2. Backward Compatibility:
 *    MINOR and PATCH updates must not break existing references.
 *
 * 3. Identity Preservation:
 *    A law’s NAME must never change across versions.
 *
 * 4. Transparency:
 *    Each version must include a CHANGELOG section.
 *
 * [VERSION RULES]
 * - MAJOR: Breaking changes or structural redesigns.
 * - MINOR: New features or sections.
 * - PATCH: Small corrections or clarifications.
 *
 * [CHANGELOG FORMAT]
 * Each version must include:
 *   - VERSION NUMBER
 *   - DATE
 *   - SUMMARY OF CHANGES
 *
 * [DEPRECATION]
 * - Deprecated laws must be marked clearly.
 * - Deprecation does not imply deletion.
 *
 * [COMPLIANCE]
 * All governance artifacts must follow this law to ensure predictable
 * evolution and stable interoperability.
 *******************************************************************************
 * [END AVIS.ARTIFACT]
 *******************************************************************************/
